  "title": "Days, months and telling time",
  "note": "Clock times use 〜時 (o'clock) and 〜分 (minutes), and 半 is half past. Mark a specific time or day with に: 七時に, 日曜日に. Relative words like 今日, 明日 and 毎日 take no に. Watch 四時 yoji, 九時 kuji, 四月 shigatsu and 九月 kugatsu. Months are simply number + 月.",
